I'm Margalit, a postdoc in LIDS/IDSS at MIT. I'm fortunate to be advised by [https://www.mit.edu/~rakhlin/ Sasha Rakhlin]. I'm broadly interested theoretical machine learning and high dimensional probability, and recently my research has focused on deep learning theory.

Before MIT, I was Last year, I was a postdoctoral fellow at the Simons Institute in the [https://simons.berkeley.edu/programs/modern-paradigms-generalization Modern Paradigms in Generalization] program. 
In 2024, I completed my PhD in Computer Science at Stanford university, advised by [https://sites.google.com/site/marywootters/ Mary Wootters] and [https://ai.stanford.edu/~tengyuma/ Tengyu Ma]. Before coming to Stanford, I studied Math with Computer Science (18C) at MIT.

{{<span style="color:red"> I will be on the academic job market in Fall 2026/Spring 2027 for jobs starting in Fall 2027. </span>}}

